theory.intro:
A side-by-side column graph shows two groups for each category, drawn as two bars next to each other. A legend tells you which shade is which group.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large},scale=0.72]
\draw[->] (0,0)--(0,8.0); \draw[->] (0,0)--(7.4,0);
\foreach \y/\lab in {2/2,4/4,6/6} {\draw (-0.15,\y)--(0,\y); \node[left,font=\small] at (-0.15,\y) {$\lab$};}
\node[left,font=\small] at (-0.15,0) {$0$};
\draw[fill=gray!35] (0.8,0) rectangle (1.6,5); \draw (1.6,0) rectangle (2.4,3);
\draw[fill=gray!35] (4.0,0) rectangle (4.8,4); \draw (4.8,0) rectangle (5.6,6);
\node[below,font=\small] at (1.6,0) {A}; \node[below,font=\small] at (4.8,0) {B};
\draw[fill=gray!35] (0.6,7.0) rectangle (1.0,7.4); \node[right,font=\small] at (1.05,7.2) {Group 1};
\draw (3.4,7.0) rectangle (3.8,7.4); \node[right,font=\small] at (3.85,7.2) {Group 2};
\node[rotate=90] at (-1.4,4) {Value};
\node[below] at (3.2,-1.0) {Category};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

